{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Rank","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.tannaka_rankOne_gives_jetTowerChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.tannaka_rankOne_gives_jetTowerChain","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L216-L225","doc":"**Direct-route bridge (PROVED, modulo the open Tannakian class).** If the direct\nTannakian reconstruction premise holds and the rank-1 flag `hRankOne` is given, the\ntensor-generation order is total — the jet-tower chain, obtained without the\n`LieAlgebra.rank` detour. Sorry-free; the sole open input is\n`TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator.single_generator_of_tannaka_rankOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator.single_generator_of_tannaka_rankOne","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L214-L214","doc":"Direct reconstruction content: a rank-1 Tannaka dual `⊗`-generates `Rep(G)` from a\nsingle fundamental object. Open — no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L211-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.TannakianRankOneSingleGenerator","kind":"class","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L200-L214","doc":"**Direct Tannakian-reconstruction premise (OPEN — uninhabited class).** For a neutral\nTannakian category whose Tannaka dual `G` (a `Prop`-flagged rank-1 datum\n`hRankOne`) reconstructs `Rep(G)`, the fundamental-object generating set `S` is a\nsubsingleton — `Rep(G)` is `⊗`-generated by one object, *without* passing through the\nLie-algebra rank. The field is the genuine implication (`hRankOne → Subsingleton S`),\nnot `True`. **No instance is provided** — this is the honest open state of the direct\nroute (Tannakian reconstruction + rank-1 highest-weight classification, absent from\nMathlib). Kept separate from `RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator` as an independent\n(duplicate-permitted) angle.\n\n-- Ref: Deligne–Milne, *Tannakian Categories*, LNM 900; Fulton–Harris §23 (rank-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.rankOne_gives_jetTowerChain'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.rankOne_gives_jetTowerChain'","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L163-L173","doc":"**Fully self-contained variant.** Same composition, but the subsingleton⟹total step is\ndischarged *internally* by the local sorry-free `singleGenerator_forces_genTotal`\ninstead of being threaded. This exhibits that the chain half really closes with no\nhidden gap: the sole unproved input remains the open class\n`RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.rankOne_gives_jetTowerChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.rankOne_gives_jetTowerChain","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L145-L161","doc":"**Full composition (PROVED, modulo the one open class): rank-1 ⟹ jet-tower chain.**\nThreads together the open rep-theory premise `RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator` and the\nlanded order lemma (as the explicit hypothesis `subsingleton_forces_total`): *if* the\nLie algebra has rank `≤ 1`, then the tensor-generation order on the fundamental weight\nmonoid `S → ℕ` is **total — the jet tower is a chain**.\n\nThis is the exact tie between representation theory and the landed order-theoretic\nseparation `atomicity_is_jet_tower_totality` (PR #4285): rank-1 (rep side) collapses\nthe tensor-generation order to a chain (order side). The **only** unproved input is the\nopen class `RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator`; the implication itself is sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.singleGenerator_gives_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.singleGenerator_gives_chain","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L131-L143","doc":"**Decoupled tie: single generator ⟹ tensor-generation chain.** Given the landed\nsubsingleton⟹total lemma `subsingleton_forces_total` **threaded as an explicit\nhypothesis** (so this file does not import the unmerged PR #4285 branch) and a single\nfundamental object `hgen : Subsingleton S`, the free tensor-generation order on\n`S → ℕ` is total. Proved sorry-free; it is the concrete rep-theory→order composition\nstep. (The threaded hypothesis is discharged by the landed\n`QOU.Atomicity.subsingleton_forces_freeGen_total`, or locally by\n`singleGenerator_forces_genTotal` above.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator.single_generator_of_rankOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator.single_generator_of_rankOne","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The genuine content: a rank-`≤1` Lie algebra forces a single fundamental object\n(subsingleton generating set). This is the open premise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.RankOneImpliesSingleGenerator","kind":"class","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L104-L127","doc":"**Conditional class (§3b-cond): rank-1 Lie algebra ⟹ single fundamental object.**\nThe standard reductive fact that a rank-1 root datum has a single fundamental weight,\nso `Rep(G)` is tensor-generated by one fundamental object — **absent from Mathlib**\n(see survey). Axiomatized as a `Prop`-valued class whose single field is the\n**genuine implication** `LieAlgebra.rank R L ≤ 1 → Subsingleton S`, where `S` indexes\nthe fundamental objects generating `Rep(G)` for the group `G` with Lie algebra `L`.\n\nThe field is *not* `True` and *not* the file's own conclusion (the chain): it is the\nload-bearing rep-theory step `rank-1 ⟹ one generator`. `S` is fixed independently of\n`L`, so an instance must actually *prove* that a rank-1 Lie algebra forces the\nfundamental-object set to a single element — the whole content of the highest-weight\nclassification in rank 1.\n\n**OPEN PREMISE — no instance is provided.** Per `AGENTS.md §\"Axiomatization is NOT a\nProof\"`, declaring this class does **not** prove `rank-1 ⟹ single object`; the\ntheorem is mathematically open in this corpus. Downstream results depending on it are\n*rigorous conditionals*, never unconditional claims.\n\n-- Ref: Fulton–Harris §11–§14, §23; Bourbaki, Lie VIII (see file docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.singleGenerator_forces_genTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.singleGenerator_forces_genTotal","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L87-L100","doc":"**Single fundamental object ⟹ tensor-generation order is total (a chain).**\nIf the fundamental-object index set `S` is a subsingleton (one generator), the free\ntensor-generation order on `S → ℕ` is total. A local sorry-free re-proof of the\nlanded `subsingleton_forces_freeGen_total` (PR #4285), so the chain step is genuinely\nclosed inside this file (not merely assumed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.genLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.RankOneToSingleObject.genLe","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneToSingleObject.lean#L79-L85","doc":"**Free tensor-generation order** on the weight monoid `S → ℕ` of a category with\nfundamental-object index set `S`: `genLe f g` says every fundamental multiplicity of\n`f` is `≤` that of `g` — i.e. the simple with weight `f` is a tensor factor of the\none with weight `g`. This is the local, self-contained copy of the landed\n`QOU.Atomicity.piGenLe` (PR #4285); kept here so this file does not import the\nunmerged branch. ","signatureChunk":0}]}